{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 400}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 100, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 3 leaves only edge 4 feeding the output (or disconnects it), causing collapses like exp 190."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a missing edge 0 reconnects node 1 and adds a strong conv path, giving large gains (exps 219, 262, 337, 152)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping a parameter-free pooling on the final edge for a conv adds learnable capacity directly at the output (exps 6, 34, 65, 310, 324)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading the input-to-output pooling edge to a 3x3 conv helps much more than replacing skip or 1x1 conv (exps 28, 263, 156 vs 126, 243)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on edge 1 with a 3x3 conv consistently gives gains of several points (exps 101, 115, 329, 265)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Losing the strongest conv on the edge feeding the output into pooling removes capacity and degrades accuracy (exps 64, 223)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on edge 0 strips the main computation into node 1, while removing a skip there can even help (exps 57, 283 vs 81, 299)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on the direct input-output edge with pooling causes large drops (exps 202, 387, 238, 321)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cutting a skip on edge 2 removes the path that lets node-1 features reach node 2, hurting consistently (exps 240, 261, 288)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip where edge 1 was absent improves gradient flow, but replacing a conv with skip loses capacity (exps 293, 327, 363 vs 49, 342)."}], "tok": 51138, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [2, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none"], [2, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "none"], [0, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [2, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [0, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none